# Vadhyar stack and evidence rules

- V1: one prepared NovaDesk TypeScript workspace, one ownership requirement and an archived-milestone transfer task.
- Current authorization: professional GitHub presentation, portable browser installer and reviewed local updates; the user explicitly authorized pushing. Preserve historical S7 evidence; never force-push.
- The learner edits source; the runtime coach has no edit, shell or arbitrary-command tool.
- Use strict TypeScript, Vitest and one root npm lockfile; add later dependencies only when needed.
- The fixture intentionally checks client role without ownership; label its baseline behavior honestly.
- Keep approval logic pure and shared with future preview/check consumers; simulated actors are not authentication.
- Use React/native VS Code APIs for the future panel, esbuild/Vite for bundles, Zod at external boundaries and the official OpenAI SDK.
- Keep requirement documents in the project; snapshots/sessions belong in workspace extension storage.
- Store API credentials only in SecretStorage; never send them to the webview or child processes.
- Preview bounded context before transmission; exclude secrets, tests/solutions, dependencies, generated and unrelated files.
- Host-issued source IDs resolve only to allowlisted real paths and valid current line spans.
- Graph relationships are proposed interpretations confirmed by the learner, not proof of requirement satisfaction.
- Require Workspace Trust and the prepared scenario before execution; use fixed executables, arguments, check IDs and timeouts.
- Fingerprint requirement/source/check/config identities; dirty buffers block runs and concurrent edits invalidate results.
- Reject edited check definitions; distinguish failure, error, timeout, stale, refusal and malformed output.
- The runner determines verification status; render model text safely with no executable links or HTML.
- Record predictions before counterexamples, hint use and guided versus unassisted transfer attempts.
- Persist records atomically, preserve valid evidence after failure and delete only Vadhyar-owned session data on request.
- Do not claim mastery, authorship or learning gains from checkpoints or rehearsed demos.
